## Traffic
Sender: evidence/vsend.py (scapy 2.6.1, sudo) — 100 frames per burst, dst 00:00:5e:00:53:ff (unknown
unicast -> flooded), payload marker CKVLAN-<burst>-<seq>; ip10 = IPv4 192.168.10.1->192.168.10.2/UDP,
ip20 = 192.168.20.1->192.168.20.2/UDP, ipx = EtherType 0x8137, ipv6 = 2001:db8::1->::2/UDP, other =
EtherType 0x88b5. Captures: tcpdump -w, filter `ether src <sender MAC>`, counted by evidence/vcount.py
(tags read from the 802.1Q headers). Counters: `show interface <ports> | include Interface|output packets`
read before the first burst and after each burst (raw in evidence/18252-step1.out, -step2.out).
Background on these ports during the run (measured from the burst-free intervals): port3.0.13 ~+60,
port1.0.2 ~+60, port4.0.9 ~+50, port4.0.26 ~+20, port1.0.9 ~+10, port1.0.13 ~+10 per ~10 s read
interval — bench vlan-1 chatter; the test deltas below are the raw delta minus that background.

## STEP 1 — send to case port1.0.1 (= DUT port3.0.13, from eth1, src 00:00:5e:00:53:01), 14:34:10-14:34:51
Expected: 192.168.10.x -> port1.0.2, port1.0.3(=1.0.9), port1.0.5(=4.0.9); 192.168.20.x -> 1.0.2,
1.0.4(=1.0.13), 4.0.9; IPX like 10.x; IPv6 like 20.x; other -> 1.0.2 and 4.0.9 (vlan 1).
Host captures (evidence/18252-s1-eth3.pcap, 500 frames; 18252-s1-eth2.pcap, 200 frames):
  eth3 (DUT trunk port1.0.2 via x230):  100 s1ip10 tags=210 0x0800 | 100 s1ip20 tags=220 0x0800 |
       100 s1ipx tags=210 0x8137 | 100 s1ipv6 tags=220 0x86dd | 100 s1other tags=none 0x88b5
  eth2 (DUT access-220 port1.0.13 via SA): 100 s1ip20 untagged 0x0800 | 100 s1ipv6 untagged 0x86dd — nothing else
DUT output-packet deltas per burst (raw delta / minus background):
  burst   p1.0.2      p1.0.9      p1.0.13     p4.0.9      p4.0.26     p3.0.13(ingress)
  ip10    +160/100    +110/100    +10/0       +150/100    +20/0       +60/0
  ip20    +160/100    +10/0       +110/100    +150/100    +21/0       +61/0
  ipx     +164/100    +112/100    +12/0       +154/100    +21/0       +63/0
  ipv6    +163/100    +10/0       +110/100    +152/100    +21/0       +63/0
  other   +161/100    +10/0       +10/0       +150/100    +120/100    +61/0
Verdict per line: ip10 PASS (1.0.2 tagged 210, 1.0.9, 4.0.9; not 1.0.13); ip20 PASS (1.0.2 tagged 220,
1.0.13 untagged at eth2, 4.0.9; not 1.0.9); IPX PASS (as ip10, tag 210); IPv6 PASS (as ip20, tag 220);
other PASS (untagged at 1.0.2, 4.0.9; not 1.0.9/1.0.13; also the bench's other vlan-1 port 4.0.26 — VLAN-1 flood, expected).
The case NOTE ("packet loss may occur on port1.0.4 because of the packet tagged") did not apply: the
access-220 port emitted the 220 set untagged, 100/100 at eth2.

